🧠 My Understanding

The main thing I learned today is that Amazon EKS makes it easier to run Kubernetes on AWS by managing the Kubernetes control plane while allowing us to focus on deploying, scaling, securing, and managing our applications running on the cluster.

Another important takeaway is how Kubernetes concepts that I learned earlier—Pods, Deployments, Services, Ingress, ConfigMaps, Secrets, HPA, and RBAC—can be applied to a real cloud environment using Amazon EKS.
